                  "questionHtml": "<p><b>Raccoon Scales Building</b></p>\n\n<p>A woman (28)________ on the 10th floor of an apartment building was shocked to discover a raccoon asleep on her balcony. She called experts from Skedaddle Humane Wildlife Control to come remove the animal and return it to the wild. The raccoon had (29)________ plans, though. When the team from Skedaddle <strong>(30)</strong>________, the raccoon darted to the corner of the balcony, hoisted itself over the railing, and slowly inched backward down the building. After taking a break on a fourth-floor balcony, the raccoon resumed its trip to the ground, and ran away from the apartment building.</p>\n\n<p>Larry Sorel, director of the Seneca Park Zoo in Rochester, New York, says balconies can be inviting places for raccoons to shelter, especially if food (31)________ out. &ldquo;Raccoons are great climbers – they can get almost (32)________ with their human-like hands,&rdquo; Sorel says. &ldquo;But I’m surprised this raccoon climbed quite so high!&rdquo;</p>",
